    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6090" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesēna</span></b> , ae,
		f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				town in</i> Gallia Cispadana, now <i>Cesena</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Fam. 16, 27, 2</span></i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 15, 20, §
			116</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caesēnas</span></b> , ātis,
				adj., <i>of Cœsena</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					14, 6, 8, § 67</span></i>
			.</div>
